Main Function
Although the Game class is a handy encapsulation of the game’s behavior, the entry point of any
C++ program is the main function. You must implement a main function (in Main.cpp)
as shown in Listing 1.3.
Listing 1.3 main Implementation
int main(int argc, char** argv)
{
Game game;
bool success = game.Initialize();
if (success)
{
game.RunLoop();
}
game.Shutdown();
return 0;
}
This implementation of main first constructs an instance of the Game class. It then calls
Initialize, which returns true if the game successfully initializes, and false otherwise.
If the game initializes, you then enter the game loop with the call to RunLoop. Finally, once the
loop ends, you call Shutdown on the game.
